{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"OPEN_ACCESS:Y AND HAS_FT:Y AND DOI:10.1186/s13059-019-1832-y","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"31727128","source":"MED","pmid":"31727128","pmcid":"PMC6857279","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC6857279"]},"doi":"10.1186/s13059-019-1832-y","title":"OrthoFinder: phylogenetic orthology inference for comparative genomics.","authorString":"Emms DM, Kelly S.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Emms DM","lastName":"Emms","firstName":"David M","initials":"DM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Plant Sciences, University of Oxford, South Parks Road, Oxford, OX1 3RB, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Kelly S","lastName":"Kelly","firstName":"Steven","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8583-5362"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Plant Sciences, University of Oxford, South Parks Road, Oxford, OX1 3RB, UK. steven.kelly@plants.ox.ac.uk."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8583-5362"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","wikipedia","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"20","journalIssueId":2875650,"dateOfPublication":"2019 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":2019,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Genome Biol","title":"Genome biology","essn":"1474-760X","issn":"1474-7596","isoabbreviation":"Genome Biol","nlmid":"100960660"},"printPublicationDate":"2019-11-01"},"pubYear":"2019","pageInfo":"238","abstractText":"Here, we present a major advance of the OrthoFinder method. This extends OrthoFinder's high accuracy orthogroup inference to provide phylogenetic inference of orthologs, rooted gene trees, gene duplication events, the rooted species tree, and comparative genomics statistics. Each output is benchmarked on appropriate real or simulated datasets, and where comparable methods exist, OrthoFinder is equivalent to or outperforms these methods. Furthermore, OrthoFinder is the most accurate ortholog inference method on the Quest for Orthologs benchmark test. Finally, OrthoFinder's comprehensive phylogenetic analysis is achieved with equivalent speed and scalability to the fastest, score-based heuristic methods. OrthoFinder is available at https://github.com/davidemms/OrthoFinder.","affiliation":"Department of Plant Sciences, University of Oxford, South Parks Road, Oxford, OX1 3RB, UK.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Evaluation Study","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Royal Society","grantId":"UF140484","orderIn":0},{"agency":"European Research Council","grantId":"637765","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genomics","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Phylogeny"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Algorithms"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Software"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Comparative genomics","Gene duplication","Gene Tree Inference","Ortholog Inference"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-019-1832-y"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC6857279"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC6857279?pdf=render"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"P